<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Antilles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Antilles are the islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> colonised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from the 1620s, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and spreading to Guadeloupe, Martinique and smaller islands. In the 17th century a governor-general, most famously <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phillippe-de-longvilliers-de-poincy">Philippe de Longvilliers de Poincy</a>, oversaw them from Saint Kitts. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar plantations</a> worked by enslaved Africans became the basis of their economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-antilles.jpg" alt="French Antilles" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gd21091993 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:French_Antilles.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
